From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hz-xiaxz <1806656034@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:57:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(login): log in and check login state on a page that is
 not redirected to rednote
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From overseas IPs www.xiaohongshu.com/explore (and /explore/<id>,
/user/profile/...) now 302 to www.rednote.com, which has its own login
state. The QR login window therefore logged into rednote (shown as an
"unknown" device in the app's device list, while xiaohongshu web logins
show as Windows 10), and the status check on /explore always saw a
guest. Repeated attempts then hit the web device limit
("电脑设备登录超限").

Login, FetchQrcodeImage, CheckLoginStatus and WaitForLogin now use the
search result page, which is not redirected and shows the xiaohongshu
QR modal to guests, and read __INITIAL_STATE__.user (loggedIn /
userInfo.guest) instead of the /explore sidebar, keeping the sidebar
selector as a fallback. Login no longer panics via MustElement when the
page goes away, and FetchQrcodeImage returns the navigation error instead of
panicking (TestLoginQrcodeClosesBrowserOnNavigationPanic → ...Failure: it
now asserts an error and still checks that the browser profile is gone).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
